msgid "Welcome to Big WindowMaker"
msgstr ""

msgid "Get to know your new desktop."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Welcome to Big WindowMaker! Click an icon to learn about it. Use Next to "
"continue."
msgstr ""

msgid "A classic"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Window Maker is a window manager inspired by NeXTSTEP, created by Alfredo "
"Kojima in 1997: simple, fast and elegant. Big WindowMaker brings it to "
"BigLinux, in an X11 session (Window Maker) and a Wayland one (wlmaker)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Main menu"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Right-click on an empty spot of the desktop to open the main menu: programs, "
"appearance, settings and the session. Drag its title bar to keep it open."
msgstr ""

msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Drag the title bar to move a window and the bottom bar to resize it. The "
"left button minimizes it, the right one closes it. Double-click the title to "
"roll the window up; right-click the title for its menu, with Maximize."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dock"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Dock keeps your favorite programs. Double-click an icon to open the "
"program; drag a running program's icon onto the Dock to keep it there."
msgstr ""

msgid "Clip"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Clip, the paperclip at the top left, changes the workspace with its "
"arrows and holds programs that belong to a workspace."
msgstr ""

msgid "Shortcuts"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The key combinations of this session, as they are configured now. Click Open "
"to see the list."
msgstr ""

msgid "Welcome"
msgstr ""

msgid "First Steps"
msgstr ""

msgid "Make Big WindowMaker your own."
msgstr ""

msgid "Here are the essential settings. Select an item and click Open."
msgstr ""

msgid "WPrefs"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Customize menus, windows, the Dock, shortcuts and the behavior of Window "
"Maker."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On Wayland, what wlmaker understands from WPrefs is applied automatically: "
"appearance, keys, mouse, focus and hot corners."
msgstr ""

msgid "Monitors"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Resolution, refresh rate, rotation and arrangement of the monitors, with "
"profiles that come back at login and when the same monitors are plugged in. "
"Applying asks for confirmation and goes back by itself after 15 seconds."
msgstr ""

msgid "Keyboard and mouse"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Key repeat, mouse speed and double-click are in WPrefs. The language and the "
"keyboard layout follow the system, chosen during installation."
msgstr ""

msgid "Accessibility"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Locate the pointer by shaking the mouse, the on-screen keyboard and the dark "
"theme. Animations of this tutorial follow the system setting to reduce "
"motion."
msgstr ""

msgid "Add/Remove Software"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Install, update and remove programs: from the BigLinux repositories, the AUR "
"and Flatpak. Also in the main menu: Settings > Add/Remove Software."
msgstr ""

msgid "Default browser"
msgstr ""

msgid "Choose the browser that opens links."
msgstr ""

msgid "Light and dark"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Switch the whole desktop between the light and the dark theme: windows, "
"menus, GTK and Qt programs."
msgstr ""

msgid "Meet Window Maker"
msgstr ""

msgid "Discover the tools that make this desktop special."
msgstr ""

msgid "Select a tool to see it in action."
msgstr ""

msgid "WMDock"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Keep your favorite programs at hand and follow important information through "
"the dockapps."
msgstr ""

msgid "Tabbed Dock"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Programs and shortcuts in tabs, at the bottom of the screen, inspired by "
"OPENSTEP. Click a tab to change it; drag a program to keep it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Customize the look and the behavior of Window Maker."
msgstr ""

msgid "wmake-zones"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Arrange windows in zones or automatic tiling. While you drag a window, a "
"panel shows the layouts: first the layout, then the zone."
msgstr ""

msgid "wmcliphist"
msgstr ""

msgid "The clipboard history: what you copied stays in a list to use again."
msgstr ""

msgid "wmshutdown"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Shut down, restart or suspend from the dockapp's button. This tutorial never "
"does it for you."
msgstr ""

msgid "The most useful key combinations of this session."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dockapps"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The little programs of the Dock: a clock, the processor, the memory, the "
"network, the volume. Each one fits in a tile."
msgstr ""

msgid "Window Maker"
msgstr ""

msgid "Community and About"
msgstr ""

msgid "Be part of the evolution of Big WindowMaker."
msgstr ""

msgid "Big WindowMaker is made in the open. Select an item to take part."
msgstr ""

msgid "GitHub"
msgstr ""

msgid "See the source code, follow the development and find what is new."
msgstr ""

msgid "Contribute"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Report a problem, suggest an improvement, help with translations or with the "
"code: everything starts with an issue."
msgstr ""

msgid "Support"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Big WindowMaker is made with dedication and collaboration. If you like the "
"project, you can contribute voluntarily: Pix key {pix}. Click Copy to copy "
"it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Developers"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Big WindowMaker: Rafael Ruscher and Barnabé Di Kartola. Window Maker: "
"Alfredo Kojima, Dan Pascu and the Window Maker Team. wlmaker: Philipp "
"Kaeser. Built on BigLinux."
msgstr ""

msgid "Alfredo Kojima"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Big WindowMaker is also a tribute to Alfredo Kojima, creator of Window "
"Maker, whose work helped preserve the elegance and simplicity of desktops "
"inspired by NeXTSTEP."
msgstr ""

